# Raw/derived pipeline data -- large, and fully regenerable by re-running the
# pipeline (see README.md / PROJECT_NOTES.md). Not committing these keeps the
# repo small and avoids GitHub's 100MB per-file hard limit outright (the raw
# dump alone is 200MB+).
proofwiki-dump.xml
proofwiki-dump.xml.gz
proofwiki_graph.graphml
graph_nodes.json
graph_edges.json
page_titles.json
redirect_map.json
core_graph.json
cluster_hierarchy.json
viz_data.json
wiki_pages/

# viz_data.json's contents are already inlined into explorer.html (the actual
# shareable deliverable), so nothing of value is lost by not tracking it
# separately.

# Debug/sample scratch output, not real project content
_cluster_sample.txt
_defof_check_result.txt
_sample_*.txt

# Runtime artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code's own local tooling -- not part of the shipped project
.claude/
.cc-history/

# A separate, unrelated project living in this same directory -- not part of
